    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Drake Baldwin** (69.51) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Drake Baldwin** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Singer, whose 4.68 xERA is the softest we will face today; batting leadoff, **Drake Baldwin** is positioned to maximize his run-scoring potential. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** capitalizes on the same target, Dobnak, utilizing a strong platoon advantage to secure his high efficiency score. While **Henry Bolte** (59.84) sits just outside the \"Strong\" threshold, he remains a high-upside play, bolstered by a significant +10% park factor adjustment that makes him our most dangerous threat for a stolen base breakout today.\n\nWe are forced to navigate several tough matchups against elite arms, which has depressed the scores of our cornerstones. Both **Kyle Tucker** (53.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.39) face Pivetta and Glasnow respectively; while their raw projections are high, the steep negative adjustments for facing such high-tier pitching (xERA 3.27 and 3.05) keep their scores in the marginal range. **Wade Meckler** (42.97) serves as our most difficult bench decision, ultimately falling short due to a park factor penalty against Woo. We are keeping a close eye on **Heliot Ramos** (47.70); while his score is dragged down by the elite delivery of Seymour, his 88% sprint speed indicator offers a rare chance to chase points in our league's scarcest category, SB, despite the difficult matchup. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Gunnar Henderson** currently unavailable due to injury or scheduling, the success of the Austin Waves today rests on **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung** providing professional, high-floor at-bats to stabilize our 5x5 Roto performance.",
